1: # PIPD-LS-SP — Pre-Implementation / Pre-Dev Lifecycle Skills Plugin
2: 
3: A governed, contract-first toolkit for the **pre-implementation** stage of a project: it turns a
4: stated intent into a validated chain of machine-readable artefacts — PI → PD →
5: ConstructionContract → ECP / TQAEP — each bound to one of **19 canonical JSON Schema families**,
6: and it refuses to hand you something it cannot check. It ships **8 skills** and a **13-command
7: CLI** (`init` `intake` `profile` `compile-pi` `bind-pd` `compile-ecp` `compile-tqaep` `validate`
8: `doctor` `project` `export` `diff` `repair`) that produce and verify those artefacts
9: deterministically.
10: 
11: Licensed **Apache-2.0**. This repository is an owner-authorised open-source **preview / beta**, not
12: a production release — read [Claim ceiling](#claim-ceiling) before building on it.
13: 
14: ## Start here
15: 
16: | | |
17: |---|---|
18: | **Installable preview** | tag **`v0.1.0-preview.2`** — Apache-2.0 |
19: | **Release page** | https://github.com/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/releases/tag/v0.1.0-preview.2 |
20: | **Download the tag, not the branch** | `main` now carries the repaired code, but a branch tip is a moving target. The **immutable** bytes are the tag's. |
21: | **Superseded** | `v0.1.0-preview.1` — still downloadable, but it ships the two defects described below. Use `.2`. |
22: | **What is not claimed** | [Claim ceiling](#claim-ceiling) and the release notes |
23: 
24: ## Choose your path: CLI or Skills
25: 
26: The published wheel and a chat-host skill pack are **two different artefacts with two different
27: boundaries**. Pick the one your job needs — installing the wheel does not make the eight logical
28: skills appear in a web chat host, and mounting the pack does not put `pipd` on your machine.
29: 
30: **CLI / headless harness** — download the immutable wheel published under the **`v0.1.0-preview.2`**
31: tag (`pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl`; published digest
32: `d6c3e295f817b50108b1232a120564c18b517864ad1ad19c4f8d915f396d364f`, verified against the tag's
33: `SHA256SUMS`). Install with **Python >= 3.11** into a **virtual environment**, then run `pipd doctor`.
34: The wheel carries the Python **13-command CLI** and the **19 installed schemas**; it does **not**
35: install or auto-load the eight logical skills into a web host.
36: 
37: **Skills / document consumption** — the versioned mount pack
38: `dist/mount/PIPD-LS-SP_S4_WEB_MOUNT_v0.1.0-preview.2.zip` (with its `.sha256` sidecar and the
39: `MANIFEST.sha256` inside the unpacked directory). It lives on this candidate branch and is **not** a
40: published release asset — there is no download URL for it here. Two sub-options:
41: 
42: - **(a) native skill uploader** — a host that has a real native skill uploader could register the
43:   pack; this path is **not yet demonstrated here**.
44: - **(b) manual document / Knowledge attachment** — attach `SKILL.md` plus the short starter prompt
45:   (`PIPD_LS_SP_QUICKSTART_PROMPT.md`) to a conversation or Project Knowledge. This document path
46:   does **not** execute `pipd` on the reader's machine.
47: 
48: ## Quickstart
49: 
50: Copy-paste, from a shell. Requires **Python >= 3.11** and `curl`. The installable identity is the
51: **immutable** tag `v0.1.0-preview.2`; `main` is rolling, so pin the tag rather than the branch.
52: 
53: ### bash / POSIX
54: 
55: ```bash
56: set -e                             # stop at the first failing step; no step fails silently
57: # 1. Fetch the published wheel and the checksum list, from the immutable tag.
58: BASE=https://github.com/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/releases/download/v0.1.0-preview.2
59: curl -fsSLO "$BASE/pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl"
60: curl -fsSLO "$BASE/SHA256SUMS"
61: 
62: # 2. Verify the bytes. Check exactly what step 1 downloaded: SHA256SUMS lists three assets, but
63: #    only the wheel is present here, so select its line. This is the ONLY integrity check offered:
64: #    there is no install-time or startup cryptographic readback, and no release signature.
65: #    Published wheel digest: d6c3e295f817b50108b1232a120564c18b517864ad1ad19c4f8d915f396d364f
66: grep '  pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl$' SHA256SUMS | sha256sum -c -
67: #    expect: pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl: OK
68: #    Alternative, only after fetching EVERY asset SHA256SUMS lists, the whole file checks clean:
69: #      curl -fsSLO "$BASE/pipd-ls-sp-v0.1.0-preview.2-source.zip"
70: #      curl -fsSLO "$BASE/PREVIEW_NOTES_v0.1.0-preview.2.md"
71: #      sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS       # expect three ": OK" lines (wheel, source zip, notes)
72: 
73: # 3. Install into a virtual environment.
74: python -m venv .venv
75: . .venv/bin/activate 2>/dev/null || . .venv/Scripts/activate   # POSIX: .venv/bin/ ; Windows: .venv/Scripts/
76: python -m pip install ./pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl
77: 
78: # 4. Check the install, then use it.
79: pipd doctor                        # expect: {"verdict": "PASS", ...}
80: pipd --help                        # 13 commands
81: 
82: # 5. Start a project. Both of these lines were executed against the published wheel.
83: pipd --root ./myproject init      # -> exit 0; creates docs/ schemas/ src/ tests/ dist/
84: pipd doctor                       # -> {"verdict": "PASS", ...}, and it names the schema source it resolved
85: ```
86: 
87: ### Windows (PowerShell)
88: 
89: ```powershell
90: $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'   # stop at the first failing step; no step fails silently
91: # 1. Fetch the same wheel and checksum list, from the immutable tag.
92: $Base = "https://github.com/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/releases/download/v0.1.0-preview.2"
93: Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "$Base/pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl" -OutFile "pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl"
94: Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "$Base/SHA256SUMS" -OutFile "SHA256SUMS"
95: 
96: # 2. Verify the wheel against its published digest. SHA256SUMS lists three assets but only the wheel
97: #    was fetched, so compare the wheel's own hash to the published literal.
98: $expected = "d6c3e295f817b50108b1232a120564c18b517864ad1ad19c4f8d915f396d364f"
99: $actual = (Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 -Path "pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl").Hash.ToLower()
100: if ($actual -ne $expected) { throw "wheel SHA-256 mismatch: $actual" }
101: "pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl: OK"   # expect this line
102: 
103: # 3. Install into a virtual environment.
104: python -m venv .venv
105: if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "python -m venv failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE)" }
106: .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
107: python -m pip install .\pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl
108: if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "pip install failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE)" }
109: 
110: # 4. Check the install, then use it.
111: pipd doctor                        # expect: {"verdict": "PASS", ...}
112: if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "pipd doctor failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE)" }
113: pipd --help                        # 13 commands
114: if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "pipd --help failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE)" }
115: pipd --root .\myproject init       # --root before the subcommand (the global form)
116: if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "pipd init failed (exit $LASTEXITCODE)" }
117: ```
118: 
119: ### Unverified one-line install (no hash check)
120: 
121: If you do not need to check the bytes against the published digest, pip can fetch and install the
122: wheel in one line:
123: 
124: ```bash
125: python -m pip install "https://github.com/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/releases/download/v0.1.0-preview.2/pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl"
126: ```
127: 
128: This performs **no hash verification** - pip installs whatever the URL serves when you run it. Use
129: the verified path above when the bytes matter.
130: 
131: Beyond that the pipeline is `intake` -> `compile-pi` -> `bind-pd` -> `compile-ecp` /
132: `compile-tqaep` -> `validate`, and **the middle steps take real inputs, not free text** — verified
133: against the CLI rather than assumed.
134: 
135: ### Run it: the whole compiler chain, copy-paste
136: 
137: These are the exact commands that produced the checked-in [`examples/first-run/`](examples/first-run/)
138: fixture, run from this checkout root. For `init`, `intake`, `profile`, `compile-pi`, `bind-pd`,
139: `compile-ecp`, `compile-tqaep`, `validate` and `doctor`, `--root` is a global option and must
140: precede the subcommand; `project` and `export` **additionally** accept `--root` after the
141: subcommand. `--root <dir>` points at a workspace (use a directory outside the tree so scratch files
142: never pollute the checkout), and the fixture paths are the real files in this repository. Both
143: absolute paths below (`PY`, `PYTHONPATH`) are pinned for this environment — adjust them to your
144: interpreter and checkout; any Python >= 3.11 with `jsonschema` works:
145: 
146: ```bash
147: PY=/c/Users/user/AppData/Local/Programs/Python/Python311/python.exe   # any Python >= 3.11 + jsonschema
148: export PYTHONPATH="C:/Projects/Agent_Workspace/PIPD-postrelease-wt/src"   # this checkout's src/
149: ART="C:/Users/user/AppData/Local/Temp/pipd-first-run"    # a scratch dir OUTSIDE the checkout
150: rm -rf "$ART" && mkdir -p "$ART"
151: CTX="$ART/ctx"; mkdir -p "$CTX"          # the read-only dir bind-pd probes (empty -> stable)
152: 
153: "$PY" -m pipd_ls_sp.cli --root "$ART" init                 # exit 0; creates docs/ schemas/ src/ tests/ dist/
154: 
155: # intake: compile source clauses into an IntentCard (typed refusal if the source does not exist)
156: "$PY" -m pipd_ls_sp.cli --root "$ART" intake \
157:   --goal "Compile this example clause source into a validated PI to PD to ECP to TQAEP chain." \
158:   --source examples/first-run/source.txt \
159:   --constraint "candidate-only, no release" \
160:   --non-goal "no upstream document bodies copied" \
161:   > "$ART/intent.card.json"            # -> INTENT-9f8e9a1b6dc344fc
162: 
163: "$PY" -m pipd_ls_sp.cli --root "$ART" compile-pi \
164:   --intent "$ART/intent.card.json" --profile LITE \
165:   > "$ART/pi.json"                     # -> PI-50952b3a3822b28c
166: 
167: # bind-pd derives a READ-ONLY RepoContext from --repo-root (here an empty dir, so it is stable);
168: # the same intent + the same RepoContext.root reproduce every digest byte for byte.
169: "$PY" -m pipd_ls_sp.cli --root "$ART" bind-pd \
170:   --pi "$ART/pi.json" --repo-root "$CTX" \
171:   > "$ART/pd.json"                     # -> PD-336c387a7aa71c9d
172: 
173: "$PY" -m pipd_ls_sp.cli --root "$ART" compile-ecp \
174:   --pd "$ART/pd.json" --pi "$ART/pi.json" \
175:   > "$ART/ecp.json"                    # -> ECP-73cf63e34806711a
176: 
177: "$PY" -m pipd_ls_sp.cli --root "$ART" compile-tqaep \
178:   --pi "$ART/pi.json" --ecp "$ART/ecp.json" \
179:   --maker HERMES-MAKER --checker GLM-5.3-FLASH-AO-LANE --checker-receipt deleg_example/lane-C \
180:   > "$ART/tqaep.json"                  # -> TQAEP-2bf7b7e31b820fb7 (claim ceiling TQAEP_DESIGNED)
181: 
182: # The 13-command CLI has no "assemble" verb, so bundle the four records with the checked-in helper.
183: "$PY" examples/first-run/assemble_bundle.py \
184:   "$ART/pi.json" "$ART/pd.json" "$ART/ecp.json" "$ART/tqaep.json" > "$ART/bundle.json"
185: 
186: # validate: schema + semantic invariants over two schema records each
187: "$PY" -m pipd_ls_sp.cli --root "$ART" validate --bundle "$ART/bundle.json"
188: # -> exit 0; {"verdict": "PASS", "checked": 4, "findings": []}
189: ```
190: 
191: Every `sha256` is stable across runs: the same fixture driven twice into two fresh workspaces against
192: the same `CTX` produced identical `intent.card.json`, `pi.json`, `pd.json`, `ecp.json` and `tqaep.json`
193: (`PI`/`TQAEP` depend only on the fixture; `PD`/`ECP` also bind `CTX` — so keep `CTX` fixed to reproduce
194: them). Full digests are in [`examples/first-run/README.md`](examples/first-run/README.md). A source
195: locator that does not exist (`--source examples/first-run/missing.txt`) is refused
196: `{"code": "AUTHORITY_UNKNOWN"}`, exit `2`, with no artefact written — the CLI is deliberately strict
197: rather than guessing on your behalf.
198: 
199: Known limitation: there is **no CLI verb that assembles a bundle**, which is why the block calls
200: `examples/first-run/assemble_bundle.py` (it only re-serialises the four records). Run
201: `pipd <command> --help` for each command's real flags. `pipd doctor` is the self-check; it reports
202: which schema source it resolved and refuses to be silent about it.
203: 
204: The three `--root` forms the parser really accepts, each run from a scratch directory and observed
205: exiting `0`:
206: 
207: ```bash
208: pipd --root ./demo init                  # exit 0 — global --root before the subcommand
209: pipd project --root ./demo --dry-run     # exit 0 — subcommand-local --root (project only)
210: pipd export --root ./demo --dry-run      # exit 0 — subcommand-local --root (export only)
211: ```
212: 
213: `pipd init --root ./demo` is refused (exit `2`): `init` does not accept a subcommand-local `--root`,
214: which is the boundary the paragraph above describes.
215: 
216: ## What is in this tree
217: 
218: | path | what it is |
219: |---|---|
220: | `schemas/` | the **19 canonical machine-contract families** + `registry.json` (Draft 2020-12, `additionalProperties: false`), written by the Codex bounded writer |
221: | `src/pipd_ls_sp/` | the plugin runtime (12 modules): intake, profile binding, the PI→PD→ConstructionContract→ECP/TQAEP pipeline, deterministic validators, the 13-command CLI |
222: | `skills/` | the **8 published skills** — `pipd-route-intake`, `pipd-profile-tailor`, `pipd-pi-compile`, `pipd-pd-bind`, `pipd-execution-contract`, `pipd-assurance-tqaep`, `pipd-authority-source`, `pipd-package-project` — each with `SKILL.md`, `references/`, `schemas/` and `tests/cases.yaml` |
223: | `tests/` | deterministic tests: the S0 contract set, the LITE vertical slice, negative and adversarial cases, rollback, secret patterns, tooling guards, quarantine disposition (POS/NEG/EDGE), oracle-disagreement, evidence-MD hard-gate refusal |
224: | `tools/` | governed-round tooling: knowledge probe, HGK admission driver, kanban receipts, CLI smoke, publication manifest and attestation, destructive-destination guards |
225: | `docs/` | `S0_CONTRACT_SPEC.md` (the frozen spec that drives `schemas/`), the round disclosure records, and [`FRONT_PAGE_HISTORY.md`](docs/FRONT_PAGE_HISTORY.md) |
226: | `fixtures/` | typed negative and golden fixtures used by the tests |
227: | `examples/` | runnable fixtures: [`examples/first-run/`](examples/first-run/) is the real input the compiler walk-through above uses, and `examples/self-bootstrap/` is the self-bootstrap transcript |
228: | `openspec/` | the change proposals these rounds implemented |
229: | `dist/` | **the published build** — wheel `pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl` (SHA-256 `d6c3e295…`), its `.sha256`, `WHEEL_MANIFEST.json` and `web/` packs |
230: | `.hgk/` | the rounds' governance record: admission, kanban, knowledge index, preflight, round receipts and surfaces |
231: | `pyproject.toml` | packaging metadata (`pipd-ls-sp` 0.1.0, `requires-python >= 3.11`, `license = "Apache-2.0"`) |
232: | `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`, `OWNER_LICENSE_DECISION.yaml`, `SBOM.cdx.json` | the Apache-2.0 grant, its attribution, the owner's operative decision record (`decision: Apache-2.0`) and the machine-readable component inventory |
233: | `PROVENANCE.md`, `ACCEPTANCE.md` | how the artefacts were produced, and what was accepted |
234: | `.agents`, `.hermes`, `.gitattributes`, `.gitignore` | agent and repository plumbing |
235: 
236: ## Claim ceiling
237: 
238: Status words are kept separate on purpose, and none of them is upgraded by this page.
239: 
240: | claim | state |
241: |---|---|
242: | `PROMPT_COMPILE_PASS` | claimed locally, evidence in `.hgk/preflight/` |
243: | `HGK_ADMITTED` | claimed locally — the HGK lifecycle reached `EXECUTING` |
244: | `LOCAL_QUALIFIED` | claimed locally (deterministic tests + CLI smoke) |
245: | `RUNTIME_READY` | **NOT claimed** |
246: | `INDEPENDENT_PASS` | **NOT claimed as a full pass.** Verifiers working only from published bytes returned scoped receipts — `9/9` on the preview, `6/6` on a defect repair, and a further `PASS` on `v0.1.0-preview.2` — but the S0–S4 challenge as a whole is **`PARTIAL_CHALLENGE`**, not a full pass |
247: | `PUBLICATION_APPROVED` | **GRANTED for the limited preview only** — owner licence decision `Apache-2.0`. **`G-RELEASE_FULL_PASS` is NOT granted.** |
248: | `RELEASED` | limited to `OWNER_AUTHORIZED_OPEN_SOURCE_PREVIEW_BETA_PUBLISHED`, at the preview tags |
249: | `PRODUCTION_VERIFIED` | **NOT claimed** |
250: 
251: **Stage coverage.** S0 and S1 were reached; the S2–S4 work followed. **S5 (HGK live), S6 (GENIE),
252: S7 (JIT), S8 (SWOF/SGM), PRE-W3 and the 22 inactive external technologies are deferred.**
253: 
254: ## Known limitations
255: 
256: Stated here rather than left only on the release page, because they matter when you decide what to
257: build on this:
258: 
259: 1. **No vulnerability or supply-chain scan of this project's own source.** A dependency audit of the
260:    declared closure found no known advisories, but `pipd-ls-sp` is not on PyPI and was itself
261:    **skipped** by that audit — the dependency closure was scanned, the source was not. There is also
262:    **no lock file**, so the audited set is not necessarily the set you will install.
263: 2. **No release signature and no build attestation.** Only a published SHA-256, for manual
264:    download-consistency checking. That is not provenance, and it does not bind the artefact to a
265:    builder identity.
266: 3. **The SPEC/DEL denominator stays `28 evidenced / 10 active gaps / 19 deferred` of 57 rows.**
267:    `EVIDENCED != PASS`; not every applicable row has been individually audited.
268: 4. **`RELEASE_MANIFEST@1` (`DEL-018`)** — was `FAIL` / `EVIDENCE_GAP` on the release line and was
269:    **closed** for the published subject by regenerating the projection; that closure ships in
270:    `v0.1.0-preview.2`. **On this branch it is `PASS`.** After the repaired lineage was merged here the
271:    tree briefly had `253` product paths with one — `docs/FRONT_PAGE_HISTORY.md` — carrying no
272:    release-evidence disposition, because the **evidence manifest's seal was stale by four rounds**
273:    (bound to the R5R execute commit `9667783`) and had never enumerated a file that only ever existed
274:    on this branch's line. Re-sealing the evidence manifest from the current tree and rebuilding the
275:    projection resolved both: `--verify` exits `0`, the manifest carries `1085` entries, and
276:    `--check --current` now exits `0` with `253/253` covered and `0` violations, the file correctly
277:    disposed `NOT_PUBLISHED`. No tag moved, no release asset changed, no validator edited.
278: 5. **Native Windows symlink / junction / reparse behaviour is not certified** beyond the tested
279:    scope (`TT-R5P-01`, `TT-R5P-06`).
280: 6. **`v0.1.0-preview.1` carries two defects**, both reproduced against its published bytes:
281:    `validate` did not resolve wheel-installed schemas the way `doctor` does (it exited `2` with
282:    `INPUT_SHAPE_INVALID`, looking for `<cwd>/schemas/PI-PKG.schema.json`), and a bundle assembled
283:    from the compilers' unmodified stdout was rejected because `compile-pi` emitted a top-level
284:    `_profile_meta` that `PI-PKG` forbids. **Both are fixed in `v0.1.0-preview.2`.** A published tag
285:    is never rewritten, which is why the fix arrived as a successor release rather than an edit.
286: 
287: ## Licence
288: 
289: **Apache-2.0** (`LICENSE`, `NOTICE`). The owner granted it in round R5Q
290: (`FAR-PIPD-R5Q-LICENSE-001`); `OWNER_LICENSE_DECISION.yaml` records `decision: Apache-2.0`. The
291: grant is effective wherever this tree is checked out, including `main`.
292: 
293: ## History and evidence
294: 
295: This page is a rewrite, and it has now been rewritten twice — which is itself recorded rather than
296: hidden.
297: 
298: - **R6** replaced an append-only log (an R3 body, an R4 section, an R5Q banner, a dangling `## 8.`
299:   fragment) whose sections contradicted each other. The section that held the R3 audit-repair
300:   snapshot, and the trailing fragment, are preserved **verbatim** in
301:   [`docs/FRONT_PAGE_HISTORY.md`](docs/FRONT_PAGE_HISTORY.md).
302: - **R8** merged the repaired lineage into `main` and **re-derived every claim on this page** against
303:   the merged tree rather than carrying the previous wording over. The pre-merge text asserted five
304:   things that the merge made false — that this branch's wheel was an old R3 build, that the
305:   Apache-2.0 grant did not apply here, that `main` was not the distribution entry point, that
306:   installing from here was "the wrong thing to do", and that the defects were fixed only off-branch.
307:   A front page that keeps saying those things after the merge is worse than one that says nothing.
308: 
309: The round-by-round record stays in the tree: `docs/ROUND_DISCLOSURE.md`,
310: `docs/ROUND3_DISCLOSURE.md`, `docs/S0_CONTRACT_SPEC.md`, and the per-round receipts and registers
311: under `.hgk/`. **Nothing was deleted to make this page read better — the history is moved, not
312: removed.**
