50: - [ ] 7.1 Produce the one-page merge decision record
51: - [ ] 7.2 Prove the write credential's repository scope, or record `AUTH_BLOCKED`
52: - [ ] 7.3 Fast-forward `main` only under owner approval, then read the remote ref back
53: - [ ] 7.4 Confirm the preview.2 tag and assets are byte-identical afterwards
54: 
55: ## 8. M4 — preview.3 release gate (owner-selected only)
56: 
57: - [ ] 8.1 Owner decision: `RELEASE_PREVIEW3=YES` or `NO`
58: - [ ] 8.2 If YES: PEP 440 version strictly greater than `0.1.0`, wheel, separate mount pack, checksums
59: - [ ] 8.3 If YES: isolated install, upgrade from `0.1.0`, rollback smoke, anonymous re-download readback
60: - [ ] 8.4 If NO: record `PREVIEW3_DEFERRED` and stop; create no empty tag
1: # pipd-ls-sp-s4r2m-conditional-merge
2: 
3: ## Why
4: 
5: The 2026-10-11 external read-only challenge review
6: (`PIPD_LS_SP_S4_MVP_PostRelease_S4R2_Independent_Acceptance_and_Preview3_Gate_2026-10-11`)
7: concluded `GO_CONDITIONAL` for merging the S4-R2 repairs into `main`, `VALUE_POSITIVE / CONDITIONAL GO`
8: for a later `preview.3`, and `PARTIAL_CHALLENGE` for the machine gates. It named exactly two
9: documentation blockers before integration: the front page never routes a reader between the CLI path
10: and the Skills path, and it states the `--root` option's position more absolutely than the shipped
11: argparse surface behaves. It also required one focused, isolated regression of the frozen product
12: before any integration, and left the public wheel unchanged until an owner-selected release gate.
13: 
14: ## What Changes
15: 
16: - The front page gains one short section that separates the two consumer paths — a pinned wheel for a
17:   CLI / headless harness, and a versioned document pack for web document consumption — and states each
18:   path's real capability boundary, including that a wheel install does not load native web skills.
19: - The `--root` text is corrected to the behaviour the CLI actually has: the global position for the
20:   compile chain, and the additional subcommand-local form for `project` and `export`.
21: - One focused regression runs the six named affected test modules plus the exact-set oracles in a
22:   disposable writable clone, while the read-only checker subject keeps identical bytes.
23: - `main` receives the approved candidate through a non-rewriting fast-forward under owner approval,
24:   with a remote ref readback; `v0.1.0-preview.2` stays immutable and publicly served.
25: - A `preview.3` release gate exists but is only executed if the owner selects it.
26: 
27: ## Non-goals
28: 
29: - No 20th schema family, no 9th logical Skill, no 14th CLI command.
30: - No rewrite of the frozen S4-R2 product commit, the sealed preview tags or their assets.
31: - No S5–S8 activation, no second control plane, no competing canonical store.
32: - No re-opening of the four already-closed ProfileBinding mutants, and no version-grammar regex added
33:   ahead of a declared version contract.
34: 
35: ## Impact
36: 
37: - Affected specs: `pipd-s4r2m-conditional-merge`
38: - Affected code: `README.md`, `tests/test_s4r2m_docs_route.py`
39: - Untouched: `v0.1.0-preview.2` tag, commit and wheel; the 19-schema set; the 8 logical skills;
40:   the 13-command CLI surface.
